{
  "_doc": [
    "Frozen test-only corpus (#139E M12.4): EVERY currently-canonical NON-listener",
    "sync_pipeline chain, plus one verb-casing duplicate. No production code path",
    "reads this file.",
    "",
    "It is the SINGLE definition of 'which chains are canonical', shared by",
    "tests/test_process_emitter_parity.py (the adapter-dialect parity harness) and",
    "tests/test_sync_pipeline_adapter_cutover.py (the differential cut-over oracle), so",
    "the two suites cannot drift apart on the question.",
    "",
    "COVERAGE IS DERIVED, NOT ENUMERATED -- and this doc deliberately states no case",
    "COUNT, because a count here could only go stale. The universe is the non-listener",
    "source primitives x the target primitives x {map, no-map}, minus the pairs the",
    "builder rejects upstream. test_sync_corpus_covers_every_canonical_chain recomputes",
    "exactly that from _SYNC_PIPELINE_STAGE_PRIMITIVE, _SYNC_PIPELINE_STAGE_ALT_PRIMITIVE",
    "and the adapter's _SOURCE_STAGE_KINDS/_TARGET_STAGE_KINDS, probes every candidate",
    "through the real gate, and asserts this corpus covers precisely the canonical ones.",
    "A new stage KIND or PRIMITIVE in those tables fails the suite until this file grows.",
    "Do not re-freeze this as a hand-maintained list.",
    "",
    "Case names ARE the fingerprint: <source_primitive>[_map]_<target_primitive>, so an",
    "omission is visible by inspection. `soap_lowercase_execute` is the single sanctioned",
    "duplicate fingerprint -- the non-uppercase `execute` verb the pre-#139C canonicalizer",
    "corrupted.",
    "",
    "WHY THE DERIVATION EXISTS. #139E's first draft froze #139C's inline set verbatim: 6",
    "STAGE-KIND chains, which at the primitive level covered well under half the canonical",
    "universe, silently omitting the map-ful SOAP chain and every mixed-connector-family",
    "combination -- precisely the surface the #139A cross-role connector guard and #139C's",
    "own family-conditional canonicalizer defect live on. Live QA caught it by grading the",
    "corpus's UNIVERSE rather than its members. Reading the set could not have.",
    "",
    "`name`/`folder_name`/`anchor` are case METADATA, deliberately siblings of `config`",
    "and never inside it: SyncPipelineBuilder.lower_config drops name/folder_name",
    "(process_flow_builder.py:5497-5499) and adapt_sync_pipeline's _KNOWN_ROOT_KEYS",
    "would reject them if they ever did survive.",
    "",
    "The cases carrying an `anchor` reproduce a committed raw-byte golden under",
    "tests/fixtures/golden_xml/ -- generated through the LEGACY renderer before the",
    "#139C cut-over, so they are not self-confirming. Their name/folder_name MUST stay",
    "byte-exact or the anchored assertion is meaningless. The rest are pinned by the",
    "differential oracle alone.",
    "",
    "The WSS listener chains are NOT here: their fused `start_listen` entry has no",
    "registry key, so they stay on the legacy renderer. The coverage test still GENERATES",
    "them as candidates and asserts the gate routes them to the legacy arm -- so when #140",
    "lands start_listen and they become canonical, that test fails until this corpus grows."
  ],
